,r=5,max=5},{tree="Affliction",name="Nightfall",r=2,max=2},{tree="Affliction",name="Siphon Life",r=1,max=1,u=true},{tree="Affliction",name="Soul Siphon",r=3,max=3},{tree="Affliction",name=S[609],r=5,max=5},{tree="Affliction",name="Wrack",r=1,max=1,u=true},{tree="Demonology",name=S[433],r=5,max=5,u=true},{tree="Demonology",name=S[477],r=2,max=2,u=true},{tree="Demonology",name=S[385],r=3,max=3},{tree="Demonology",name=S[286],r=1,max=1,u=true}},order={{l1=10,l2=13,tree="Affliction",name="Suppression",r1=1,r2=4,max=5,u=true},{l1=14,l2=18,tree="Affliction",name=S[553],r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=19,l2=19,tree="Affliction",name="Grim Reach",r1=1,r2=1,max=2,u=true},{l1=20,l2=21,tree="Affliction",name=S[521],r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=22,l2=24,tree="Affliction",name="Pandemic",r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=25,l2=26,tree="Affliction",name="Nightfall",r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=27,l2=29,tree="Affliction",name="Malevolence",r1=1,r2=3,max=5,u=true},{l1=30,l2=30,tree="Affliction",name="Siphon Life",r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=31,l2=35,tree="Demonology",name=S[433],r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=36,l2=37,tree="Demonology",name=S[477],r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=38,l2=40,tree="Demonology",name=S[385],r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=41,l2=41,tree="Demonology",name=S[286],r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=42,l2=43,tree="Affliction",name="Malevolence",r1=4,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=44,l2=44,tree="Affliction",name="Grim Reach",r1=2,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=45,l2=45,tree="Affliction",name=S[481],r1=1,r2=1,max=2,u=true},{l1=46,l2=50,tree="Affliction",name=S[609],r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=51,l2=51,tree="Affliction",name="Wrack",r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=52,l2=52,tree="Affliction",name=S[481],r1=2,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=53,l2=55,tree="Affliction",name="Soul Siphon",r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=56,l2=58,tree="Affliction",name=S[601],r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=59,l2=60,tree="Affliction",name=S[589],r1=1,r2=2,max=3,u=true}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[386]},{t="p",s="legend",x=S[104],u=true},{t="h1",x="Affliction",sub=S[443]},{t="p",s="lede",x="A simple damage-over-time and Shadow Bolt playstyle with a strong TBC feel: keep Corruption, Bane of Agony and your Curse ticking, fill with Shadow Bolt and drains, and let a Succubus add steady damage."},{t="pills",list={S[391],S[423]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[546]},{t="h2",x=S[329]},{t="p",x="These stages describe a practical route toward your chosen level-60 endpoint. Train new ranks, keep a few Soul Shards, and use the leveling point order below if you want an exact sequence."},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Dots, drains and a demon"},{t="p",x="Open with Corruption and Bane of Agony, send your Imp or Voidwalker in, and finish with Shadow Bolt or your wand. |cff71d5ffSuppression (10–13) adds spell hit first, and Improved Corruption makes Corruption instant by level 18.|r Use Drain Life to recover the health you spend on Life Tap, and Drain Soul on dying enemies to collect Soul Shards."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Build the Affliction engine"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffSummon the Succubus at 20 for damage, or keep the Voidwalker for hard pulls. Improved Bane of Agony (20–21), Pandemic (22–24) and Nightfall (25–26) come first: Nightfall procs give you instant Shadow Bolts, and Pandemic doubles the critical damage bonus of your dots and drains. Malevolence and Siphon Life (30) follow, then Demonic Embrace, Demonic Aegis and Fel Vitality (31–40) make you and your demon much tougher.|r"},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Shadow Mastery and the demon package"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffDemonic Sacrifice at 41 lets you trade a demon you do not need for a lasting bonus. Malevolence reaches 5/5 at 43, Shadow Mastery 5/5 by 50 boosts every Shadow spell you cast, and Wrack at 51 adds a strong channel that also raises your other Shadow damage over time on the target by 10%. Improved Life Tap, Soul Siphon, Improved Drains and Fel Concentration finish the build at 60.|r"},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[367]},{t="h2",x=S[391]},{t="p",x=S[47],u=true},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[394]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[351]},{t="p",x=S[70],u=true},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="|cff71d5ffWrack is the Affliction capstone and needs Siphon Life; it deals heavy Shadow damage every second and makes the target take 10% more from your other Shadow damage over time, so this build takes both. Soul Siphon also boosts Wrack for each of your other Affliction effects on the target. Only 4/5 Suppression is taken, so this build gets 4% spell hit from talents.|r"},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[457]},{t="h2",x=S[375]},{t="p",x="Affliction wants hit until the cap, then spell power and critical strike. In Forever damage-over-time ticks can crit, so crit is worth much more than in Classic."},{t="h3",x=S[528]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[571],x=S[494]},{t="stat",i=2,b="Stamina",x=S[323]},{t="stat",i=3,b="Spirit",x="more health and mana from Life Tap"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Intellect",x="mana pool"},{t="p",s="small",x="Wands with Shadow damage and Spirit are good leveling picks for Affliction."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b="Hit chance",x="to 17%"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Spell power",x=S[494]},{t="stat",i=3,b=S[503],x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Haste",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Intellect",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="|cff71d5ffFour points in Suppression give 4% hit, so you need 13% from gear.|r Past the cap, hit does nothing; swap it for spell power or crit."},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[48]},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[376]},{t="h2",x=S[409]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority guide, not a fixed loop. While leveling, omit talents and spells you have not learned. Target lifespan, mana and pull size decide how many effects are worth applying."},{t="h4",x="Set up the target"},{t="p",x="Send your Succubus in first. Apply your Curse (Curse of the Elements for dungeon bosses), then Bane of Agony and Corruption. In Forever a Bane and a Curse of yours can sit on the same enemy, so you never choose between damage and utility. Skip Bane of Agony on enemies that will die before it pays off."},{t="h4",x="Fill with Shadow Bolt"},{t="p",x="Shadow Bolt is your main filler. Shadow Mastery, Malevolence and Shadow damage gear all improve it. Corruption and your drains can trigger Nightfall; when Shadow Trance appears, your next Shadow Bolt is instant, so spend it straight away."},{t="h4",x="Drain when your effects are up"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffSoul Siphon adds 12% to Drain Life, Drain Soul and Wrack for each of your other Affliction effects on the target (up to 36%), and Improved Drains adds another 20% to your drains. From 51, channel Wrack while your dots tick: it raises the damage of your other Shadow damage over time effects on the target by 10%.|r With two or three effects up, Drain Life is both a damage and a healing button. Fel Concentration keeps the channel going while you are hit."},{t="h4",x="Execute with Drain Soul"},{t="p",x="Below 20% health, the Improved Drains bonus on Drain Soul is tripled. Switch from Shadow Bolt to Drain Soul for the last part of a fight; it also refills your Soul Shards when the enemy dies."},{t="h4",x="Manage mana with Life Tap"},{t="p",x="Life Tap now scales with Spirit, not spell damage. Tap while your health is comfortable, then let Drain Life recover it. Demonic Energies also gives your demon the mana you gain. Do not tap yourself into danger just to fill the mana bar."},{t="h4",x="Handle packs and danger"},{t="p",x="Spread Corruption and Bane of Agony with mouseover macros on packs that will live long enough. Keep Fear, Death Coil and Seduction ready. Spell Lock from a Felhunter is the better choice against heavy casters."},{t="abil",names={"Corruption",S[616],S[424],"Shadow Bolt","Drain Life","Drain Soul","Life Tap","Summon Succubus"}},{t="h3",x=S[482]},{t="p",x="Shadow spell damage and general spell power come first: almost everything you cast is Shadow. Intellect adds mana and critical chance, which Pandemic rewards on dots and drains. Spirit improves Life Tap; Stamina gives you health to tap and survive. |cff71d5ffThis build has 4% hit from Suppression, so hit on gear is still useful against bosses.|r Fire-only gear does nothing for this build and is hidden in the atlas."},{t="p",x=S[54]},{t="h3",x=S[319]},{t="p",x="Carry Soul Shards for Healthstones, a Soulstone and summons, and a stack of water: Warlocks cannot conjure drinks. Create Spellstone (from 36) is a weapon imbue that adds Shadow damage and spell haste, which suits this build better than a Firestone."},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffYour Succubus is the default damage pet; with Demonic Sacrifice you can instead sacrifice the Imp for 15% more Shadow damage when you do not need a demon out.|r Swap to the Felhunter for caster-heavy dungeons, and to the Voidwalker for risky solo pulls. Bring Curse of the Elements unless another Warlock already covers it."},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[444]},{t="h2",x=S[304]},{t="p",x=S[46]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[38]},{t="macro",n=S[395],x=S[62],code=S[141]},{t="macro",n=S[434],x=S[124],code=S[154]},{t="macro",n=S[334],x=S[65],code=S[113]},{t="macro",n=S[373],x=S[77],code=S[132]},{t="macro",n=S[529],x=S[97],code=S[181]},{t="macro",n=S[495],x=S[114],code=S[172]},{t="macro",n=S[377],x=S[112],code=S[120]},{t="macro",n=S[445],x=S[106],code=S[157]},{t="macro",n=S[435],x=S[100],code=S[155]},{t="macro",n=S[368],x=S[101],code=S[189]},{t="macro",n=S[504],x=S[144],code=S[246]},{t="macro",n=S[410],x=S[102],code=S[216]},{t="macro",n=S[572],x=S[201],code=S[335]},{t="macro",n="Drain Soul execute",x="Channel Drain Soul on the hovered enemy or your target when it drops below 20%. Releasing the key does not cancel the channel.",code="#showtooltip Drain Soul\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Drain Soul"},{t="macro",n="Shadow Bolt / Shift Drain Life",x="Normal press casts Shadow Bolt at your target. Hold Shift to start Drain Life instead when you need health back.",code="#showtooltip\n/cast [mod:shift,harm,nodead] Drain Life; [harm,nodead] Shadow Bolt"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[195]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[505]},{t="h2",x=S[352]},{t="p",x=S[51]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[36]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[44]},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[378]},{t="h2",x=S[349]},{t="p",x=S[53]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[396]},{t="h2",x=S[330]},{t="p",x=S[28]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[379]},{t="h2",x=S[301]},{t="p",x=S[35]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[364]},{t="kicker",x=S[506]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[60]}}},{id="demonology",name="Demonology",token="DEMO",title="Demonology | WoW Forever Warlock Field Guide",nav={{id="overview",x=S[545]},{id="journey",x=S[421]},{id="talents",x=S[366]},{id="stats",x=S[455]},{id="combat",x=S[456]},{id="macros",x=S[442]},{id="dungeons",x=S[393]},{id="professions",x=S[422]},{id="crafting",x=S[408]},{id="questgear",x=S[384]},{id=S[364],x=S[502]}},asideNote=S[73],talentString="0200000000000000000050032312203013510550005003",ranks={{tree="Affliction",name="Suppression",r=2,max=5,u=true},{tree="Demonology",name=S[624],r=5,max=5},{tree="Demonology",name=S[385],r=3,max=3},{tree="Demonology",name=S[595],r=2,max=2},{tree="Demonology",name=S[507],r=3,max=3,u=true},{tree="Demonology",name=S[286],r=1,max=1},{tree="Demonology",name=S[602],r=2,max=2},{tree="Demonology",name="Decimation",r=2,max=2},{tree="Demonology",name=S[617],r=3,max=3},{tree="Demonology",name="Soul Link",r=1,max=1},{tree="Demonology",name=S[590],r=3,max=3},{tree="Demonology",name=S[554],r=5,max=5},{tree="Demonology",name=S[625],r=1,max=1},{tree="Destruction",name=S[369],r=5,max=5,u=true},{tree="Destruction",name="Bane",r=5,max=5},{tree="Destruction",name="Ruin",r=5,max=5},{tree="Destruction",name=S[417],r=3,max=3}},order={{l1=10,l2=14,tree="Demonology",name=S[624],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=15,l2=17,tree="Demonology",name=S[385],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=18,l2=19,tree="Demonology",name=S[595],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=20,l2=20,tree="Demonology",name=S[286],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=21,l2=22,tree="Demonology",name=S[602],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=23,l2=24,tree="Demonology",name=S[507],r1=1,r2=2,max=3,u=true},{l1=25,l2=26,tree="Demonology",name="Decimation",r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=27,l2=29,tree="Demonology",name=S[617],r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=30,l2=30,tree="Demonology",name="Soul Link",r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=31,l2=33,tree="Demonology",name=S[590],r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=34,l2=34,tree="Demonology",name=S[507],r1=3,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=35,l2=39,tree="Demonology",name=S[554],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=40,l2=40,tree="Demonology",name=S[625],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=41,l2=45,tree="Destruction",name="Bane",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=46,l2=50,tree="Destruction",name=S[369],r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=51,l2=55,tree="Destruction",name="Ruin",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=56,l2=58,tree="Destruction",name=S[417],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=59,l2=60,tree="Affliction",name="Suppression",r1=1,r2=2,max=5,u=true}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[386]},{t="p",s="legend",x=S[104],u=true},{t="h1",x="Demonology",sub=S[443]},{t="p",s="lede",x="|cff71d5ffSacrifice your Imp for Shadow damage, keep that bonus with Demonic Pact while your Succubus fights beside you, and spam Shadow Bolt behind your curse and dots, with Soul Fire as an execute.|r"},{t="pills",list={S[500],S[423]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[546]},{t="h2",x=S[329]},{t="p",x="These stages describe a practical route toward your chosen level-60 endpoint. The sacrifice-and-Pact setup only comes together at 40, so the early levels play like a normal pet Warlock."},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Learn the basics with a pet"},{t="p",x="Corruption, Bane of Agony, Immolate and Shadow Bolt carry you early. Unholy Power, Fel Vitality and Demonic Energies make your Imp or Voidwalker hit harder and live longer, which keeps downtime short."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Sacrifice and summoning"},{t="p",x="Demonic Sacrifice arrives at 20. Before Demonic Pact, summoning any demon cancels the sacrifice, so choose between a living pet and the bonus. Master Summoner makes resummoning cheap and fast. |cff71d5ffImproved Sayaad strengthens the Succubus’s Lash of Pain, Decimation turns Shadow Bolts on low-health enemies into a cheap, fast Soul Fire, Demonic Brand lets a Searing Pain mark the target for extra demon damage,|r and Soul Link plus Demonic Knowledge strengthen you while a demon is out."},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Pact, then Destruction"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffDemonic Pact completes the setup at 40: sacrifice the Imp for 15% Shadow damage, then summon the Succubus for Master Demonologist’s extra 10% Shadow damage without losing the sacrifice. The next 18 points go into Bane, Improved Shadow Bolt, Ruin and Agonizing Flames to make Shadow Bolt faster and its critical strikes bigger, and the last two buy Suppression for hit. Soul Fire is trained at 48 and becomes your execute with Decimation.|r"},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[367]},{t="h2",x=S[500]},{t="p",x=S[47],u=true},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[394]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[351]},{t="p",x=S[70],u=true},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="|cff71d5ffDemonic Sacrifice and Demonic Pact give Demonology strong baseline damage. Sacrifice the Imp (15% Shadow damage), then summon the Succubus; with Demonic Pact the sacrifice stays active, and Master Demonologist adds 10% Shadow damage while the Succubus is out. Resummoning an Imp cancels the sacrifice. Only 2/5 Suppression is taken, so this build gets 2% spell hit from talents.|r"},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[457]},{t="h2",x=S[375]},{t="p",x="Demonology values hit the most of the Warlock specs: your demon uses your hit chance, so every miss you remove helps both of you. Your demon also scales with your spell power."},{t="h3",x=S[528]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[571],x="match your build: Shadow or Fire"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Stamina",x=S[323]},{t="stat",i=3,b="Spirit",x="more from Life Tap"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Intellect",x="mana pool"},{t="p",s="small",x="Shadow or Fire damage on gear is worth much less to the other build, so match it to the school you cast."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b="Hit chance",x="to 17%"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Spell power",x="or your build’s school damage"},{t="stat",i=3,b=S[503],x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Haste",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Intellect",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Each point in Suppression lowers the hit you need from gear by 1%. Your demon inherits your spell hit and part of it as melee hit."},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[48]},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[376]},{t="h2",x=S[409]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority guide, not a fixed loop. Before Demonic Pact at 40 and Soul Fire at 48, leave out the steps you have not unlocked."},{t="h4",x="Prepare the sacrifice"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffOut of combat, summon your Imp and use Demonic Sacrifice for 15% Shadow damage. Then summon your Succubus: Demonic Pact keeps the sacrifice active, Master Demonologist adds 10% Shadow damage for you both, and Soul Link and Demonic Knowledge stay up because a demon is out. Fel Domination is not in this build, so do this before the pull.|r"},{t="h4",x="Curse and dots first"},{t="p",x="Apply your Curse (Curse of the Elements for dungeon bosses), Bane of Agony and Corruption on targets that will live long enough, then Immolate. In Forever a Bane and a Curse of yours can share a target."},{t="h4",x="Fill with Searing Pain"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffShadow Bolt is your filler: it is Shadow, so the sacrifice and Succubus bonuses apply, Bane makes it faster and Ruin makes its critical strikes much bigger. Use Searing Pain when you want Demonic Brand on the target for extra demon damage, and watch threat on bosses all the same.|r"},{t="h4",x="Execute with Soul Fire"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffBelow 35% health, Shadow Bolt (or Searing Pain) triggers Decimation: for 10 seconds Soul Fire casts 40% faster and costs no Soul Shard, and Decimation already cuts Soul Fire’s cooldown by 90%. Spam Soul Fire through the execute phase and refresh Decimation with Shadow Bolt when it is about to expire.|r"},{t="h4",x="Keep the Imp alive and fed"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffSoul Link sends 30% of your damage taken to the Succubus, and Demonic Energies heals it for part of your spell damage and gives it the mana from your Life Taps. If the Succubus dies, resummon it: the Pact keeps your sacrifice, but you lose the Succubus-based bonuses until it is back.|r"},{t="h4",x="Packs and mana"},{t="p",x="Rain of Fire and Hellfire are Fire spells and benefit from the same bonuses. Life Tap scales with Spirit. Keep Fear and Death Coil ready for emergencies."},{t="abil",names={"Searing Pain","Soul Fire","Immolate","Corruption",S[616],S[424],S[286],"Summon Imp"}},{t="h3",x=S[482]},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffShadow spell damage and general spell power come first: Shadow Bolt, Corruption and Bane of Agony are all Shadow, and your sacrifice and Succubus bonuses multiply them. Fire damage only helps Immolate and Soul Fire. Intellect adds critical chance, which Ruin makes much more valuable. This build has 2% hit from talents, so hit on gear matters against bosses.|r"},{t="p",x=S[54]},{t="h3",x=S[319]},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffKeep Soul Shards for summoning the Imp to sacrifice, Healthstones and a Soulstone; Decimation makes Soul Fire free during the execute window. Create Spellstone (from 36) is a weapon imbue that adds Shadow damage and spell haste, which suits this build better than a Firestone.|r"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffYour Succubus keeps Master Demonologist’s Shadow bonus active and adds Lash of Pain, which Improved Sayaad strengthens. Bring Curse of the Elements unless another Warlock already covers it.|r"},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[444]},{t="h2",x=S[304]},{t="p",x=S[46]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[38]},{t="macro",n=S[395],x=S[62],code=S[141]},{t="macro",n=S[434],x=S[124],code=S[154]},{t="macro",n=S[334],x=S[65],code=S[113]},{t="macro",n=S[373],x=S[77],code=S[132]},{t="macro",n=S[529],x=S[97],code=S[181]},{t="macro",n=S[495],x=S[114],code=S[172]},{t="macro",n=S[377],x=S[112],code=S[120]},{t="macro",n=S[445],x=S[106],code=S[157]},{t="macro",n=S[435],x=S[100],code=S[155]},{t="macro",n=S[368],x=S[101],code=S[189]},{t="macro",n=S[504],x=S[144],code=S[246]},{t="macro",n=S[410],x=S[102],code=S[216]},{t="macro",n=S[572],x=S[201],code=S[335]},{t="macro",n="Sacrifice, then summon Succubus",x="With your Imp out, the first press sacrifices it. Press again with no pet to summon the Succubus, which keeps the sacrifice thanks to Demonic Pact.",code="#showtooltip Demonic Sacrifice\n/cast [pet:Imp] Demonic Sacrifice; [nopet] Summon Succubus",u=true},{t="macro",n="Soul Fire / Shift Shadow Bolt",x="Normal press casts Soul Fire for the execute phase. Hold Shift for Shadow Bolt to trigger or refresh Decimation.",code="#showtooltip\n/cast [mod:shift,harm,nodead] Shadow Bolt; [harm,nodead] Soul Fire",u=true},{t="p",s="small",x=S[195]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[505]},{t="h2",x=S[352]},{t="p",x=S[51]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[36]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[44]},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[378]},{t="h2",x=S[349]},{t="p",x=S[53]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[396]},{t="h2",x=S[330]},{t="p",x=S[28]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[379]},{t="h2",x=S[301]},{t="p",x=S[35]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[364]},{t="kicker",x=S[506]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[60]}}},{id="destruction",name="Destruction",token="DESTRO",title="Destruction | WoW Forever Warlock Field Guide",nav={{id="overview",x=S[545]},{id="journey",x=S[421]},{id="talents",x=S[366]},{id="stats",x=S[455]},{id="combat",x=S[456]},{id="macros",x=S[442]},{id="dungeons",x=S[393]},{id="professions",x=S[422]},{id="crafting",x=S[408]},{id="questgear",x=S[384]},{id=S[364],x=S[502]}},asideNote="Researched 30 October 2026\nForever data only\n\nHover, focus or tap an item icon for its tooltip. Click to keep it open; Escape closes it.\n\nResearched build · 51 points.\nReference tables and tooltips are additional.",talentString="0500000000000000000502030010000000000550055103101351",ranks={{tree="Affliction",name="Suppression",r=5,max=5},{tree="Demonology",name=S[433],r=5,max=5,u=true},{tree="Demonology",name=S[477],r=2,max=2,u=true},{tree="Demonology",name=S[385],r=3,max=3,u=true},{tree="Demonology",name=S[286],r=1,max=1,u=true},{tree="Destruction",name=S[369],r=5,max=5},{tree="Destruction",name="Bane",r=5,max=5},{tree="Destruction",name="Aftermath",r=5,max=5},{tree="Destruction",name="Ruin",r=5,max=5},{tree="Destruction",name="Shadowburn",r=1,max=1},{tree="Destruction",name=S[417],r=3,max=3},{tree="Destruction",name="Conflagrate",r=1,max=1},{tree="Destruction",name=S[547],r=1,max=1},{tree="Destruction",name=S[573],r=3,max=3},{tree="Destruction",name=S[496],r=5,max=5},{tree="Destruction",name="Incinerate",r=1,max=1}},order={{l1=10,l2=14,tree="Destruction",name="Bane",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=15,l2=19,tree="Destruction",name=S[369],r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=20,l2=20,tree="Destruction",name="Shadowburn",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=21,l2=25,tree="Destruction",name="Ruin",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=26,l2=28,tree="Destruction",name=S[417],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=29,l2=29,tree="Destruction",name="Conflagrate",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=30,l2=30,tree="Destruction",name=S[547],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=31,l2=33,tree="Destruction",name=S[573],r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=34,l2=38,tree="Destruction",name="Aftermath",r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=39,l2=39,tree="Destruction",name=S[496],r1=1,r2=1,max=5,u=true},{l1=40,l2=40,tree="Destruction",name="Incinerate",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=41,l2=44,tree="Destruction",name=S[496],r1=2,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=45,l2=49,tree="Affliction",name="Suppression",r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=50,l2=54,tree="Demonology",name=S[433],r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=55,l2=56,tree="Demonology",name=S[477],r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=57,l2=59,tree="Demonology",name=S[385],r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=60,l2=60,tree="Demonology",name=S[286],r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[386]},{t="p",s="legend",x=S[104],u=true},{t="h1",x="Destruction",sub=S[443]},{t="p",s="lede",x="|cff71d5ffHard-hitting Fire spells with two instant finishers: keep Immolate up, weave Shadowburn and Conflagrate to power Shadow and Flame, fill with Incinerate, and let Ruin turn critical strikes into big hits.|r"},{t="pills",list={S[392],S[423]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[546]},{t="h2",x=S[329]},{t="p",x="Destruction feels good from the first points: faster casts, cheaper spells and harder critical hits. The leveling point order below follows the same path the build’s core takes at level 30."},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Faster casts, cheaper spells"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffBane (10–14) shortens Shadow Bolt and Immolate, and Improved Shadow Bolt (15–19) strengthens your early filler.|r Send your demon in, Immolate, then Shadow Bolt; finish low enemies with your wand to save mana."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Big crits and two finishers"},{t="p",x="Shadowburn at 20 and Ruin from 21 make critical strikes hit far harder. Agonizing Flames boosts every Destruction spell, Conflagrate adds a second instant, and Bane of Havoc at 30 lets you cleave two tough enemies. |cff71d5ffFire and Brimstone (31–33) raises Conflagrate’s critical chance, and Aftermath (34–38) adds 50% to Immolate’s initial damage.|r"},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Incinerate and Shadow and Flame"},{t="p",x="Incinerate arrives at 40 and hits harder on Immolated targets. Shadow and Flame keeps Immolate alive through Conflagrate and refunds Shadowburn’s Soul Shard, so both finishers go on cooldown. |cff71d5ffShadowburn also raises your Fire damage by 20% for 20 seconds, which this build plays around. Suppression 5/5 by 49 adds hit, then 11 Demonology points add Stamina, armor and Demonic Sacrifice at 60: sacrifice the Succubus for 15% more Fire damage.|r"},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[367]},{t="h2",x=S[392]},{t="p",x=S[47],u=true},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[394]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[351]},{t="p",x=S[70],u=true},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="|cff71d5ffThis build plays around Fire damage: keep Immolate up, use Shadowburn to keep Shadow and Flame’s 20% Fire bonus active, Conflagrate on cooldown without losing Immolate, and fill with Incinerate on Immolated targets. Sacrifice the Succubus for another 15% Fire damage once Demonic Sacrifice is trained.|r"},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[457]},{t="h2",x=S[375]},{t="p",x="Destruction wants hit until the cap, then spell power, haste and critical strike for its direct casts. Ruin and Improved Searing Pain make crits hit very hard."},{t="h3",x=S[528]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[571],x="Fire damage counts for most of your spells"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Stamina",x=S[323]},{t="stat",i=3,b="Intellect",x="mana pool"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Spirit",x="faster recovery"},{t="p",s="small",x="Fire damage is worth about two thirds of plain spell damage to this build; Shadow damage about a third."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b="Hit chance",x="to 17%"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Spell power",x="Fire damage counts too"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Haste",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b=S[503],x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Intellect",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Crit and hit are close in value. With five points in Suppression you need 12% hit from gear."},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[48]},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[376]},{t="h2",x=S[409]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority guide, not a fixed loop. While leveling, omit talents and spells you have not learned."},{t="h4",x="Open with your demon and Curse"},{t="p",x="Send your demon in, apply your Curse (Curse of the Elements for dungeon bosses), and pre-cast a Shadow Bolt so it lands together with your Immolate."},{t="h4",x="Keep Immolate up"},{t="p",x="Immolate is the only effect you must maintain. Aftermath raises its initial hit, Conflagrate needs it, and Incinerate deals 25% more to an Immolated target. With 5/5 Shadow and Flame, Conflagrate no longer consumes Immolate."},{t="h4",x="Use both finishers on cooldown"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffConflagrate grants 20% Shadow damage and Shadowburn grants 20% Fire damage for 20 seconds through Shadow and Flame,|r and Shadowburn refunds its Soul Shard instantly. Fire and Brimstone gives Conflagrate extra critical chance, which Ruin turns into very large hits."},{t="h4",x="Choose the filler for your gear"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffIncinerate is your main filler on an Immolated target: with Shadowburn’s Fire bonus and the Succubus sacrifice, your Fire spells hit hardest. Use Shadow Bolt only while Conflagrate’s Shadow bonus is up and your Shadow damage is higher. Exact level-60 priorities still need testing.|r"},{t="h4",x="Cleave with Bane of Havoc"},{t="p",x="On two tough enemies, put Bane of Havoc on the one you are not attacking; 15% of your damage to other targets also hits it. Havoc is a Bane, so it cannot share a target with your Bane of Agony. Rain of Fire and Hellfire feed it in packs, but let the tank establish threat first."},{t="h4",x="Manage mana and Soul Shards"},{t="p",x="Destruction burns mana quickly. Improved Life Tap and Spirit improve every tap; Drain Life gets the health back. Use Drain Soul on dying enemies whenever you need more Soul Shards."},{t="abil",names={"Shadow Bolt","Immolate","Conflagrate","Shadowburn","Incinerate",S[547],S[424],"Rain of Fire"}},{t="h3",x=S[482]},{t="p",x="This build uses both schools. General spell power is the safest upgrade; Fire damage strengthens Immolate, Incinerate and Conflagrate, Shadow damage strengthens Shadow Bolt and Shadowburn. Ruin doubles the value of critical strikes, so Intellect and critical chance climb in value with gear. 5/5 Suppression already gives 5% hit; haste on gear speeds up your hard casts."},{t="p",x=S[54]},{t="h3",x=S[319]},{t="p",x="Shadowburn refunds its own Soul Shard with Shadow and Flame, but keep spares for summons, Healthstones and a Soulstone. Use Create Firestone (Fire damage and critical chance) or Create Spellstone (Shadow damage and haste) to match the school your gear favors."},{t="p",x="Without Demonology points, the Succubus is the strongest damage demon and the Imp brings Blood Pact Stamina for the group. Use the Felhunter for Spell Lock in caster-heavy dungeons. Bring Curse of the Elements unless another Warlock already covers it."},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[444]},{t="h2",x=S[304]},{t="p",x=S[46]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[38]},{t="macro",n=S[395],x=S[62],code=S[141]},{t="macro",n=S[434],x=S[124],code=S[154]},{t="macro",n=S[334],x=S[65],code=S[113]},{t="macro",n=S[373],x=S[77],code=S[132]},{t="macro",n=S[529],x=S[97],code=S[181]},{t="macro",n=S[495],x=S[114],code=S[172]},{t="macro",n=S[377],x=S[112],code=S[120]},{t="macro",n=S[445],x=S[106],code=S[157]},{t="macro",n=S[435],x=S[100],code=S[155]},{t="macro",n=S[368],x=S[101],code=S[189]},{t="macro",n=S[504],x=S[144],code=S[246]},{t="macro",n=S[410],x=S[102],code=S[216]},{t="macro",n=S[572],x=S[201],code=S[335]},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Bane of Havoc",x="Place Havoc on the second enemy under your pointer without leaving your main target. It cannot share a target with your Bane of Agony.",code="#showtooltip Bane of Havoc\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Bane of Havoc"},{t="macro",n="Conflagrate / Shift Immolate",x="Normal press casts Conflagrate. Hold Shift to Immolate first; the macro does not check whether Immolate is already on the target.",code="#showtooltip\n/cast [mod:shift,harm,nodead] Immolate; [harm,nodead] Conflagrate"},{t="macro",n="Shadowburn finisher",x="Keep your instant Shadow finisher on its own key. With Shadow and Flame its Soul Shard is refunded, so it can be used on cooldown.",code="#showtooltip Shadowburn\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Shadowburn"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[195]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[505]},{t="h2",x=S[352]},{t="p",x=S[51]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[36]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[44]},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[378]},{t="h2",x=S[349]},{t="p",x=S[53]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[396]},{t="h2",x=S[330]},{t="p",x=S[28]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[379]},{t="h2",x=S[301]},{t="p",x=S[35]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[364]},{t="kicker",x=S[506]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[60]}}}},dungeons={{n=S[361],lr="13–18",st=S[78],no=S[21],ba=true,ra={ck=S[133],r={},t={},no={S[49],S[55],S[34]}}},{n=S[240],lr="13–18",st=S[78],no=S[21],ba=true,ra={ck=S[133],r={},t={},no={S[49],S[55],S[34]}}},{n=S[152],lr="15–20",st=S[78],no=S[21],ba=true,ra={ck=S[133],r={{n="Lordaeron Captain",st="Reported Forever rare",no=S[61],it={}}},t={{id=286980,n=S[593],mob=S[26],st=S[175],no=S[42]},{id=286979,n=S[569],mob=S[26],st=S[175],no=S[42]},{id=286978,n=S[594],mob=S[26],st=S[175],no=S[42]}},no={S[34]}}},{n=S[199],lr="17–24",st=S[78],no=S[21],ba=true,ra={ck=S[133],r={{n=S[420],st=S[71],no=S[72],it={{id=5243,n="Firebelcher"},{id=6632,n=S[607]}}}},t={},no={S[55],S[34]}}},{n=S[217],lr="17–26",st=S[78],no=S[21],ba=true,ra={ck=S[133],r={{n="Miner Johnson",st=S[71],no=S[61],it={}}},t={{id=1929,n=S[520],mob=S[26],st=S[32],no=S[13]}},no={S[34]}}},{n=S[170],lr="22–30",st=S[78],no=S[21],ba=true,ra={ck=S[133],r={{n="Deathsworn Captain",st=S[71],no=S[61],it={}}},t={{id=2292,n=S[600],mob=S[26],st=S[32],no=S[13]},{id=1974,n=S[565],mob=S[26],st=S[32],no=S[13]},{id=1484,n=S[606],mob=S[26],st=S[32],no=S[13]}},no={S[34